course: dictionary
lesson: 14622
title: A portent is a sign
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A portent is a sign that something important is going to happen, often a warning that something bad is coming. «The dark clouds were a portent of the storm.» The clouds come first and the storm follows, so the clouds are the portent.
explain: Portent is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in books, news and old stories. In myths, people saw a comet or a black cat as a portent of doom. «The strange red comet was an evil portent, the villagers said.» Look for the clues: a sign, a warning, something that comes before.
explain: Be careful: science teaches that these signs do not really tell the future. A comet does not cause bad luck, and a black cat cannot bring doom. Portent can also mean serious importance: «a matter of great portent» is something very important.
fact: A portent is a sign or warning that something important is going to happen.
fact: «A portent of doom» is a sign that something terrible is coming.
fact: Portent can also mean a strange or wonderful thing that seems to carry a message.
fact: «A matter of great portent» means something of serious importance.
fact: Science teaches that signs like comets and black cats do not really foretell the future.
exercise: «The dark clouds were a portent of the storm.» What is a portent here? | *A sign that a storm is coming | A loud noise | A cloud that is pretty | A cold wind
exercise: Old stories say a black cat is an evil portent. What does evil portent suggest? | A cat that sings | *A sign of something bad to come | A cat that is very tired | A sign of a lucky day
exercise: «The old stories spoke of a portent in the sky: a bright, silent comet.» Copy the word that means a sign. | comet | sky | bright | *portent
test: «The villagers saw the strange comet as a portent of change.» What does portent of change mean? | A map of the village | A sign that nothing will ever happen | A dance for the summer | *A sign that big changes are coming
test: «The matter was of great portent, so the king called a meeting.» What does portent mean here? | *Serious importance | A small, silly game | A tiny thing nobody noticed | Rainy weather
exam: «Ella said the black cat was a portent of doom, but her teacher said science shows it cannot foretell the future.» What does the teacher's view show? | *Signs like black cats do not really tell the future | Portents are only found in science books | Portents are always wonderful | Black cats always bring doom
